  "scope": [
    "Synthesize retained Temple validation evidence into explicit findings about value, overhead, failure modes, and project-size fit without treating test count as success.",
    "Define and implement measurable Lean, Standard, and High-Assurance workflow profiles with evidence-based escalation, bounded context, relevant-Skill retrieval, and role-appropriate model guidance.",
    "Represent completed no-go or inconclusive experiments separately from active blocked delivery, and expose the distinction in human-facing status and Management Console projections.",
    "Prepare a representative multi-Agent, multi-repository microservice benchmark with a pure-local protocol rehearsal before any new model-backed execution."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "A source-linked retrospective reproduces existing Token, latency, correctness, intervention, and protocol-failure facts and labels unsupported conclusions explicitly.",
    "Low-risk bounded work can select Lean Mode without traversing unnecessary gates, while escalation preserves Independent QA and Release authority for higher-risk work.",
    "A concluded no-go experiment is terminal and historical, while a blocked delivery item remains actionable; status, Observer, Console, and tests agree.",
    "Model routing assigns Sol to consequential planning and evaluation, Terra to ordinary delivery, Luna to bounded mechanical work, and applies the same routing to both benchmark arms.",
    "The benchmark measures recovery, conflicts, rework, human intervention, Token attribution, latency, and correctness; no generation runs until its local schema and fixture rehearsal pass."
  ],
